  "worked_solution": "To calculate the initial position, we substitute $t=0$ it into the equation $s(t)=(2t+1)^{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{0} & =s(0) \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 0+1)^{3} \\\\  & ={1}^{3} \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((2t+1)^{3}) \\\\  & =6(2t+1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=0\\,\\text{s},$ we substitute $t=0$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{0} & =v(0) \\\\  & =6(2\\cdot 0+1)^{2} \\\\  & =6(1)^{2} \\\\  & =6\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
